<title>UK: BP sets June LPG price at $173/$159 a tonne.</title>
<headline>BP sets June LPG price at $173/$159 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum has announced its June price for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG), the BP Agreed Price or BPAP.</p>
<p>The propane price will be $173 a tonne, up by $18 a tonne from the May level of $155 a tonne. And butane will be $159 a tonne, a rise of $3 from the May level of $156 a tonne.</p>
<p>The price is effective from June 1.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
